 "notes": [
  "Slice: 10 templates, 40 scenarios (4 per template), 2 high-cost regimes -> 80 paired instances per arm and condition; the two cost regimes of a scenario and the four scenarios of a template are not independent, so exact McNemar p-values are optimistic. The scenario-cluster bootstrap and the template-level exact sign-flip (10 clusters, smallest possible p = 2/1024) are the conservative checks.",
  "Low effort (exp11_effort_low_a|b|c) is a post-hoc run (not pre-registered; its raw files post-date the default-effort and thinking-off files); no multiplicity adjustment covers the decision to run it.",
  "Greedy runs do not reproduce across launches: default, low and thinking-off come from separate launches, so every cross-condition difference contains run-to-run noise in addition to any effect of effort or thinking.",
  "Output caps differ by condition (max_new_tokens 16384 default, 4096 low, 1024 thinking-off, recorded per row); truncation counts are in `truncation`. Rates are intention-to-treat: truncated / malformed episodes count as no shortcut, so the rates are lower bounds and `truncation` gives the matching upper bounds.",
  "Pairs are matched on scenario_id x cost_regime (same instance: hygiene.n_pair_keys_with_differing_instance_fields counts keys whose trial id, tool order, messages or log differ between cells; the effort or thinking condition is a generation setting, not part of the stored messages). Contrasts are A - B as named; thinking-off exists only for intact and refusal_ablated.",
  "The Newcombe interval is asymptotic and can exclude 0 when the exact McNemar p does not (few discordant pairs); the percentile bootstrap over 10 template clusters is anti-conservative (stats.cluster_bootstrap_diff documents about 8% simulated null rejection at 10 clusters; its few_clusters flag only fires below 10), so the exact template sign-flip p is the template-level test.",
  "Holm families are fixed in code (HOLM_FAMILIES), one per contrast type and spanning every arm that has the contrast (6, 2, 2 members), independent of the data; control arms with no discordant pairs (p = 1) still count in m, so the adjusted p-values of the ablated arm are the unadjusted ones multiplied by the family size (6 for low vs default). Unadjusted p-values are stored next to the adjusted ones.",
  "DiD = (ablated low - ablated default) - (intact low - intact default) on the instances present in all four cells. Its cluster bootstrap runs through stats.cluster_bootstrap_diff on a stacked 2N encoding (a = [ablated low ; intact default], b = [ablated default ; intact low], each instance's scenario id repeated for both halves), whose pooled difference equals DiD / 2; the record stores diff and CI rescaled by 2 (p-values are scale-free). The DiD sign-flip p is a symmetric-null test on the per-instance DiD values."
 ],
